f. monitoring and reporting.

Article 13

(1) Increasing Community Participation as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (3) point e is to provide the widest possible opportunity for the community to participate in assisting the prevention and handling of gender-based violence and violence against children.

(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) can be carried out by:

a. providing protection for victims; b. providing emergency assistance;
c. providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding the handling of gender-based violence and violence against children cases;
d. assisting the process of submitting an application for the determination of protection;
e. providing assistance in the form of money, goods, or services; and/or
f. conveying information to the authorities related to cases of gender-based violence and violence against children.

Article 5

(1) In providing protection to victims of gender-based violence and children, the Regional Government is obligated to:

a. prevent the occurrence of violence;
b. provide protection for victims of violence;
c. provide recovery services and social reintegration for victims;
d. encourage and increase community participation;
e. cooperate with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence;
f. supervise the provision of services to victims involving the community; and
g. provide a safe house (shelter).
(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based violence and violence against children;
b. facilitate the implementation of integrated services;
c. provide facilities and infrastructure;
d. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
e. coordinate and cooperate in the provision of protection to victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
f. encourage community participation; and g. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) The Regional Government in carrying out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives, or other persons who are legally responsible to the victim.

Article 3

The objectives of this Regional Regulation are:

a. to prevent all forms of gender-based violence in the home, and violence against children occurring in the household and/or community;
b. to provide services and protection; c. to provide legal assistance;
d. to pursue recovery and social reintegration; and
e. to provide a sense of security to victims.

Article 10

Recovery Efforts and Social Reintegration as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (3) point b include:

a. providing physical recovery at health service institutions;
b. medicolegal services;
c. assisting the repatriation of victims;
d. providing protection at a Safe House (shelter), social rehabilitation center, or other place desired by the victim;
e. providing psychosocial recovery and accompaniment;
f. providing spiritual guidance services; and
g. preparing families and communities, economic empowerment, and return to school and/or other educational institutions.

Article 4

(1) Every victim of gender-based violence and children has the right to:

a. obtain protection for personal, family, and property security, and freedom from threats related to information that will be, is being, or has been provided;
b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
c. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;
d. obtain integrated services that are fast, appropriate, comfortable, and according to needs;
e. recovery and social reintegration; and
f. obtain legal, psychological assistance, spiritual guidance, economic, social and interpreter.
(2) The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

